^PARSING ERROR$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.base.init]/3, [dcl.init.list]: a mem-initializer argument list may
have a braced-init-list element.  CBMC's parser rejected a leading braced-init-
list argument followed by more arguments in a mem-initializer ( `m({a,b}, t)` );
rMemberInit's `( {` special case parsed only a single braced-init-list and then
required `)`.  Fixed by parsing the full argument list via rFunctionArguments
(which accepts braced-init-list elements).  Unblocks refined_string_exprt's
`: struct_exprt({_length, _content}, type)` (src/util/string_expr.h).
